menu "AI engine"

    choice AI_RUNTIME
        prompt "Inference runtime"
        default AI_RUNTIME_TFLM
        help
            Which runtime this image builds and links; the other one's code
            stays in the tree for the comparison of KEHOACH 3 layer 5. The
            models partition must carry files of the same runtime.

        config AI_RUNTIME_TFLM
            bool "TFLite Micro with esp-nn"

        config AI_RUNTIME_ESPDL
            bool "ESP-DL"
    endchoice

    config AI_WEIGHTS_PSRAM_DETECT
        bool "Copy the detection weights into PSRAM"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_ESPDL && SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            ESP-DL copies the parameters out of the flash mapping when it
            builds the graph (param_copy), and reads them over octal PSRAM
            instead of quad flash. Measured faster on every model tried
            (KEHOACH 3 layer 5); n reads them in place and spends no PSRAM.

    config AI_WEIGHTS_PSRAM_SPOOF
        bool "Copy the anti-spoof weights into PSRAM"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_ESPDL && SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            As for detection.

    config AI_WEIGHTS_PSRAM_RECOG
        bool "Copy the recognition weights into PSRAM"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_ESPDL && SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            As for detection.

    config AI_ARENA_FAST_KB
        int "Ceiling for the detection arena (KB)"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_TFLM
        default 224
        range 16 2048
        help
            Detection is the only branch that runs on every frame, so it gets
            an arena to itself (KEHOACH 3.8). The size comes from the image:
            models_0 carries arena_hint per entry, and this only caps it, so a
            model of another size needs no rebuild. Used when the image says 0.

    config AI_ARENA_FAST_INTERNAL
        bool "Ask for the detection arena in internal SRAM"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_TFLM
        default n
        help
            Internal SRAM buys detection 23.3 ms per frame, but the 224 KB it
            costs leaves the LCD bounce buffer and the Wi-Fi stack short by
            156 KB (KEHOACH 6.4). Turn this on once the models shrink enough
            for that budget to close. The arena falls back to PSRAM, loudly,
            when it does not fit.

    config AI_ARENA_BIG_KB
        int "Ceiling for the anti-spoof and recognition arena, PSRAM (KB)"
        depends on AI_RUNTIME_TFLM
        default 1536
        range 64 8192
        help
            Both run only once a face appears, rarely enough for PSRAM, and
            they share one MicroAllocator so their heads overlap while their
            tails stack (KEHOACH 3.8). Each of the two entries carries the pair
            total in arena_hint and the engine takes the max; this only caps it.

    config AI_PROFILING
        bool "Report ticks per operator after every invoke"
        default n
        help
            TFLM: turns on the MicroProfiler, which costs roughly 48 KB of
            static RAM and a print per invoke; E8-T8 uses it to tell an operator
            with an ESP-NN kernel from one running the reference C path.
            ESP-DL: every invoke runs through profile_module and prints the
            latency of each module, sorted.

endmenu
